{"units": [{"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote231", "translation": "For this will not suffice to prevent him from falling dishonorably."}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote232", "translation": "I will not endure not honoring the city."}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote233", "translation": "those nearby (or: to those nearby)"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote234", "translation": "the affairs of those outside"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote235", "translation": "the most seemly of the present"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote236", "translation": "those beneath the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote237", "translation": "greatest herald of those above and below"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote238", "translation": "those hereafter"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote239", "translation": "formerly"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote240", "translation": "the good"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote241", "translation": "the opposite"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote242", "translation": "before"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote243", "translation": "the things from there"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote244", "translation": "the things from outside"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote245", "translation": "most of all, added by an interpolator"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote246", "translation": "the things before"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote247", "translation": "the things from there"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote248", "translation": "the things from there"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote249", "translation": "the things beyond"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote250", "translation": "because of the excessive love of mortals"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote251", "translation": "to the gods of old"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote252", "translation": "you accomplished the former need"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote253", "translation": "of the words of old"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote254", "translation": "of the former night"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote255", "translation": "such a misfortune for you in addition to the former one"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote256", "translation": "and of the former luxury"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote257", "translation": "of the help at that time"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote258", "translation": "the vain burden"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote259", "translation": "of mortals of the present"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote260", "translation": "the custom of parents before"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote261", "translation": "of the former entrances"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote262", "translation": "the former prosperity"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote263", "translation": "of the former toils"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote264", "translation": "and I will show the present as trustworthy proofs, where Hermann restored γονέων ἐπιδείξω, which the scholiast seems to have read."}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote265", "translation": "the watcher from on high"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote266", "translation": "according to the laws from home"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote267", "translation": "the divinities here"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote268", "translation": "and the divinities here"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote269", "translation": "the former track"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote270", "translation": "knowing the affairs of those outside"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote271", "translation": "the affairs of those outside are best increased"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote272", "translation": "knowing well the affairs of the enemy"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote273", "translation": "the affairs of this man"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote274", "translation": "the affairs of the Persians"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote275", "translation": "the affairs of the masters"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote276", "translation": "and the honors of the chthonian gods, where τὰ is corrupted from a"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote277", "translation": "the affairs of the natives"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote278", "translation": "not to admire the things of the gods"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote279", "translation": "but the woes among mortals"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote280", "translation": "the contest around herself"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote281", "translation": "to some husband from heaven"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote282", "translation": "to those outside the walls"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote283", "translation": "and to the friends beneath the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote284", "translation": "the gods under the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote285", "translation": "the things upon these"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote286", "translation": "the griefs in the houses at the hearth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote287", "translation": "of the Achaeans—those from the army"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote288", "translation": "the time through eternity"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote289", "translation": "but the things into your mind"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote290", "translation": "the cloak of the earth below"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote291", "translation": "and the danger to you at Troy"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote292", "translation": "the torch-lit processions weeping around you"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote293", "translation": "of Hades under the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote294", "translation": "the solace of the Chryseids, those at Troy"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote295", "translation": "by the lamentations from the house"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote296", "translation": "of those at Zygos"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote297", "translation": "the word from the heart"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote298", "translation": "the divinities beneath the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote299", "translation": "of the gods under the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote300", "translation": "the spinner from the deep"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote301", "translation": "the one in the house"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote302", "translation": "but the sword near the lungs"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote303", "translation": "and to the friends beneath the earth, and to those above"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote304", "translation": "the fear from dreams"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote305", "translation": "the lots among men"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote306", "translation": "fleeing the former time"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote307", "translation": "for the errors from former times"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote308", "translation": "the things among men"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote309", "translation": "to those under the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote310", "translation": "all the divinities throughout the city"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote311", "translation": "the places beneath and below the earth"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote312", "translation": "the proofs from me"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote313", "translation": "the reverence from the gods"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote314", "translation": "the thing from the women"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote315", "translation": "the divinities around the Nile"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote316", "translation": "the station above the fire"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote317", "translation": "we honor Hermes, the race around the lake"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote318", "translation": "my heart is torn by fear, oā oā, of the Persian army."}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote319", "translation": "and the city of the Cissians will sing in answer, oā oā, this word, the crowd full of women crying out. In these two places in M a simple oâ is read, written thus, not bá, which is in the copies. I doubled it, following examples of other exclamations of this kind."}]}